Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Align repo with paper: network encryption, TTL
 kill-clock, example policy pack

- infra_data_platform: add aws.directconnect.Connection with MACsec
  (request_macsec + must_encrypt) on the AWS-facing hop of the Megaport
  bridge - Megaport's Vxc resource has no encryption property of its own,
  so this is the actual mechanism behind the paper's 'encrypted end-to-end
  by the primary cloud provider' claim.

- infra_ml_compute: add pulumiservice.TtlSchedule (+ required
  DeploymentSettings) as a fixed-duration kill-clock. Closes the gap where
  a silently-hung workload (no crash, no exit code) was never reclaimed -
  the existing failure trap only fires on a non-zero exit. Extension based
  on an in-container health signal is documented as an explicit,
  unimplemented extension point (same pattern as the existing .done-marker
  assumption), not built here.

- policy-pack-example/: new minimal PolicyPack (S3 public-access block,
  GPU pod resource limits) wired into train.yml via
  `pulumi up --policy-pack`, demonstrating the paper's shift-left policy
  mechanism. Explicitly marked illustrative, not a compliance statement -
  both example policies check things the repo's stacks already do
  correctly.

- README: documents all three additions in place, updates the pipeline
  diagram and repo structure tree accordingly.
